The above mentioned glazes are examples of glazes which have been developed and have been in production for a certain period, mainly in the 70ties and 80ties of last century. Besides these glazes many more glazes like these were developed in the same way. The glazes are examples of how a certain surface, colour or effect can be realized by making use of the 'free space' in the glaze formulae. This way of working could only be done by the glaze manufacturers as basic red, yellow and cadmium frits have never been free available on the commercial market.

From the basic frits there have been developed various standard cadmium selenium glazes which were directed already into a specific application, e.g. for normal twice firing, for high firing / once firing, suitable for wall- or floor tiles, for vases, giftware, white or coloured bodies, etc.

